<description>
Attach monochrome sprites to the matching sides of a central hollow square.

Input structure:
- bg = background. A hollow NxN square (hub) with bg corners/interior and four differently-colored edges (top, bottom, left, right).
- 2-4 monochrome sprites scattered on the grid, each matching one hub edge color.

Rule:
- For each hub edge color, find the matching sprite outside the hub.
- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).
- Translate it to adjoin that hub side. 
- Clear everything else to bg; output is hub + attached sprites only.

Key insight: Each edge color uniquely pairs a sprite to a side; symmetry along the contact-edge axis disambiguates the correct rotation.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "solid monochrome sprite s",
  "dst": "attach to an edge of hollow polychrome sprite d with bg corners and 4 differently-colored side edges",
  "match_cond": "s.head.color == d.edge.color and s.head.length == d.edge.length",
  "transform": "rotate s to align matching edge with d.side"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 18-26 rows x 20-26 cols, bg=8 [observed]
  dst (hub):
    shape: NxN hollow square, N in 3-6 (solver range); N=4 in all examples [observed]
    structure: |
      . T T .      corners = bg, interior = bg
      L . . R      each side = (N-2) cells of one solid color
      L . . R      4 sides use 4 distinct non-bg colors
      . B B .
    position: near grid center (solver picks candidate closest to center)
    edge_len: N-2 (= 2 when N=4)
  src (sprites):
    count: 2-4 matching sprites + 0-1 distractors
    matching: one monochrome sprite per hub-edge color; color uniquely pairs sprite to side
    missing_sides: 0-2 sides may have no sprite (only hub edge shown, nothing added in output)
    connectivity: 8-connected (may be only diag-connected; solver uses 8-conn labeling)
    symmetry: in attached orientation, sprite is symmetric perpendicular to contact axis (fliplr for top/bot attach, flipud for left/right attach); required by solver
    contact_edge: exactly N-2 contiguous filled cells on the attachment side of the rotated sprite
    rotation: solver tries rot90 x 0-3; exactly 1 rotation should be valid (avoid rotationally symmetric shapes that create ambiguity)
    pixels: 4-12 [observed], bbox height 2-4, width 2-6 [observed]
    placement: scattered far from hub and each other (Chebyshev gap >= 3 [observed])
    orientation: placed in a random rotation different from the attached orientation
    distractors: 0-1 sprites in a non-edge color; ignored by solver, absent from output
  output:
    same grid dims; bg everywhere except hub + flush-attached sprites
    each matched sprite rotated and translated so its contact edge touches the corresponding hub side
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first then scatter
  steps:
    - Pick grid H, W, hub size N (use 4), bg color (8)
    - Choose 4 distinct non-bg colors for hub edges; place hub near center with margin >= max sprite extent + 2 on all sides
    - Choose K sides (2-4) to get sprites; for each side, design a monochrome sprite mask satisfying the symmetry and contact-edge constraints, ensuring exactly 1 valid rotation
    - Build output by attaching each sprite flush against its hub side; verify no overlap between attached sprites
    - Derive input by detaching each sprite, applying a random non-identity rotation, and placing it at a random location with Chebyshev gap >= 3 from hub and other sprites
    - Optionally add 0-1 distractor sprite in a fresh non-edge color
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

